{"kind":"request","text":"Please review chess item 2, the host binding implementation, at exact head 135c4826168c04d7a520e8a644c9dab12d684884 (branch request/chess-item2-host-binding, pushed; worktree left in place). It is assigned work under request git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:5682b41417a18d585ab5efda7e48753bcd8a8232, and the design authority is the ratified note notes/2026-08-13-second-application.md, delivery item 2, together with layer 4 Application host binding in docs/reference/architecture.md. Record the three conclusions. Architecture: the head touches internal/app (host selection and init-time binding) and adds kernel.ReadOpening, a bounded authenticated read that is explicitly not a verification; I judge the layer 4 and layer 1 contracts preserved and so changed no contract page, and I would like that judgement checked. Security: the binding is read only from the opening records, only from the key that initialized the repository, with an unauthorized or later binding-shaped record passed over rather than raised so nobody who can append can make a repository unreadable; opening commits are checked for the sequencer signature, first-parent chaining from the configured genesis, actor signature, genesis target, and payload binding; payloads must be canonical JSON with no unknown fields; a dirty build records no source commit. Simplification: I already dropped a registration helper whose only caller was a test. Two choices I want challenged: a workroom repository records no binding at all, because absence names workroom permanently and recording one would change the opening of every workroom log and break the zero-behaviour-change condition, at the cost of not pinning source commit and fold version for workroom; and the fold-version and application refusals are carried as a cached selection error rather than an Open failure, so the repository stays kernel-verifiable. Gates at the exact head: go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test ./... -count=1, green across all 25 packages, with the existing internal/app tests unmodified. The candidate artifact is stale in the ordinary reasoning sense because both of its bases are, but it is not world-stale.","body":{"conditions":"independent A/S/S review of exact head 135c4826168c04d7a520e8a644c9dab12d684884 against candidate git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c74384fde3286e9dab42e53c4ef77ed2e6062463; approval authorizes claude to merge with step-5 succession at internal/app","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}